# Normalise line endings in the repository, so the stored form does not depend on
# whoever happened to commit.
#
# Text files are stored as LF and checked out in whatever is native to the machine.
# Without this, the behaviour comes from each contributor's local core.autocrlf: a
# clone with different settings can rewrite every line ending in a file on a one-line
# edit, which buries the real change in the diff and ruins git blame for that file.
* text=auto

# Belt and braces. Git normally detects this as binary on its own, but the client mod
# archive is what the server hands to joining players and what the updater fetches, so
# it must never be eligible for line-ending conversion.
*.zip binary
